Some macOS checks follow the macOS Security Compliance Project
(https://github.com/usnistgov/macos_security), CC BY 4.0.

Vulnerability data is downloaded at run time from OSV (https://osv.dev) and
reduced to package names, affected version ranges, fixed versions, ids and
severity. Its sources and licenses are listed at
https://google.github.io/osv.dev/data/; for the ecosystems used here:
GitHub Advisory Database (https://github.com/github/advisory-database),
CC BY 4.0; PyPI Advisory Database (https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database),
CC BY 4.0; Python Software Foundation Database
(https://github.com/psf/advisory-database), CC BY 4.0; Go Vulnerability
Database (https://github.com/golang/vulndb), CC BY 4.0; RustSec Advisory
Database (https://github.com/rustsec/advisory-db), CC0 1.0. Each finding names
the advisory ids it is based on.
